  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crafting future by Sustainable Livelihoods, protection and Gender equality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will reach 3870  Households (13000 individuals) with special focus on Rohingya and host community peoples. This project is an integrated approach where include of food security and livelihood, protection and gender dynamics. There are three project outcomes. Outcome 1: Improved livelihoods through access to income for the Rohingya and host women, reducing disaster risks, and enhancing the healthy environment of camps and host locations. Outcome 2: Rohingya and host women and youths are proficient at taking community actions to respond to protection concerns and disaster preparedness. Outcome 3: Women are empowered in challenging harmful social norms and negotiating for rights resulting from transformative and feminist leadership intercession. This action will be directly implemented by Oxfam. This project will connect and capacitate Munda Households (HHs) with organisation development (self -help group) for linkages with Government Organisation  - Non Government Organisation (GO -NGO) service providers and to fight climate shocks and threats.</narrative>
  </description>
